1
00:04:14,285 --> 00:04:20,285
Eloise at the Plaza is a comedy, family, mystery film directed by Kevin Lima.

2
00:08:28,571 --> 00:08:34,571
Eloise is a precocious but lovable six-year-old girl
who lives in New York's Plaza Hotel.

3
00:12:42,857 --> 00:12:48,857
Her caretaker "Nanny" watches over her while her mom is away.

4
00:16:57,142 --> 00:17:03,142
Then one day, while trying to figure out how to get invited to a fancy ball as well as
how to meet a visiting prince, Eloise makes a new friend around her age!

5
00:21:11,428 --> 00:21:17,428
So she decides to take him on a tour of the city - and all while
plotting some matchmaking hijinks for her other friends too!

6
00:25:25,714 --> 00:25:31,714
Eloise, played by Sofia Vassilieva.

7
00:29:40,000 --> 00:29:46,000
Leon, played by Kintaro Akiyama.

8
00:33:54,285 --> 00:34:00,285
Nanny, played by Julie Andrews.

9
00:38:08,571 --> 00:38:14,571
Sir Wilkes, played by Kenneth Welsh.

10
00:42:22,857 --> 00:42:28,857
Mr. Salomone the Manager, played by Jeffrey Tambor.

11
00:46:37,142 --> 00:46:43,142
Miss Thompson the Main Desk Attendant, played by Tannis Burnett.

12
00:50:51,428 --> 00:50:57,428
Eloise at the Plaza is a 2003 American comedy television film based on the Eloise series of
children's books written by Kay Thompson and illustrated by Hilary Knight.

13
00:55:05,714 --> 00:55:11,714
It stars Sofia Vassilieva as Eloise, a mischievous six-year-old girl who lives
in the penthouse at the top of the Plaza Hotel in New York City.

14
00:59:20,000 --> 00:59:26,000
Julie Andrews, Jeffrey Tambor, Kenneth Welsh, Debra
Monk, and Christine Baranski also star.

15
01:03:34,285 --> 01:03:40,285
The film was directed by Kevin Lima, written by Janet Brownell, and produced by
HandMade Films and DiNovi Pictures for Walt Disney Television.

16
01:07:48,571 --> 01:07:54,571
Filming took place in Toronto and New York City.

17
01:12:02,857 --> 01:12:08,857
It aired on ABC on April 27, 2003, as an episode
of The Wonderful World of Disney.

18
01:16:17,142 --> 01:16:23,142
A sequel, Eloise at Christmastime, aired that November.

19
01:20:31,428 --> 01:20:37,428
The film explores themes of hotel, new york city, nanny, prince, little girl.

20
01:24:45,714 --> 01:24:51,714
The tone is lighthearted and mind_bending.
